# Every path in this repo requires review from the owner below.
#
# Canonical: standards/repo-baseline/files/.github/CODEOWNERS in
# cfoforit-claude-plugins. Do not edit in place.
#
# This file is `templated`, not `exact`: the EXTRA-PATHS variable is substituted per repo
# with that repo's own top-level directories, and the renderer appends the owner to each
# one. NEVER write a placeholder in double braces anywhere in this file, comments
# included: the renderer does not distinguish a comment from a rule, so a multi-line value
# lands at column 0 and every line after the first reads as a path entry.
#
# In CODEOWNERS the last matching pattern wins, and a pattern with NO owner CLEARS
# ownership. A bare path line therefore removes the protection this file exists to grant,
# which is why the owner is appended per line rather than left to the default rule above.
#
# The OWNER is asserted separately by the manifest's `owner_must_be`, so a well-formed file
# that names the wrong approver is a distinct and higher-severity finding than a formatting
# difference. That both those checks pass says nothing about whether every path line names
# anyone: that is a third check, and it is the one this file was failing until 2026-09-01.

